# Configuration file for fw_(printenv/saveenv) utility.
# Up to two entries are valid, in this case the redundant
# environment sector is assumed present.
# Notice, that the "Number of sectors" is ignored on NOR and SPI-dataflash.
# Futhermore, if the Flash sector size is ommitted, this value is assumed to
# be the same as the Environment size, which is valid for NOR and SPI-dataflash

# NOR example
# MTD device name	Device offset	Env. size	Flash sector size	Number of sectors
#/dev/mtd1		0x0000		0x4000		0x4000
#/dev/mtd2		0x0000		0x4000		0x4000

# MTD SPI-dataflash example
# MTD device name	Device offset	Env. size	Flash sector size	Number of sectors
#/dev/mtd5		0x4200		0x4200
#/dev/mtd6		0x4200		0x4200

# NAND example
#/dev/mtd3		0x120000		0x1000		0x20000			2

# 2026-07-31: this board's U-Boot environment does NOT live on NAND --
# stock's own config above was a leftover from before this project
# confirmed CONFIG_ENV_IS_NOWHERE (env/nowhere.c, no save/load at all)
# was silently discarding every saveenv on this build. A CONFIG_ENV_IS_IN_MMC
# switch (raw sector on the SD card, /dev/mmcblk0 offset 0x40000) was
# tried the same day but REVERTED after hardware-testing found it hangs
# the board completely before even "DRAM:" prints (root cause not yet
# found -- see docs/DEVICE_TEST_CHECKLIST_2026-07-18.md §83). Currently
# back on CONFIG_ENV_IS_NOWHERE, meaning U-Boot's environment genuinely
# has NO persistent storage at all right now -- there is no correct
# value for this file to point at. Left commented below (not deleted)
# for whenever CONFIG_ENV_IS_IN_MMC gets a proper re-attempt.
#/dev/mmcblk0		0x40000		0x40000
